    description: "UAT 2026-04-13 UX-03+UX-04: (a) `hypergumbo foobar` reports 'Error: path does not exist' — the parser treats unrecognized words as path arguments. Should suggest valid subcommands. (b) `hypergumbo sketch . --debug` fails with 'unrecognized arguments'; correct syntax is `hypergumbo --debug sketch .`. Either accept `--debug` after subcommand or improve the error message. Both are argparse plumbing issues; fix together."  # 4718
